  "question": {
    "text": "Which one of the following carbonyl compounds cannot be prepared by addition of water on an alkyne in the presence of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HgSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>?</mo></math>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<img src=\"assets\\ot1_0094_d7598af6ca5d.png\" style=\"width: 129px; height: 51px;\" />",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<img src=\"assets\\ot2_0094_33cd241aa5d6.png\" style=\"width: 127px; height: 52px;\" />",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<img src=\"assets\\ot3_0094_1cb0d6ba9fa9.png\" style=\"width: 86px; height: 47px;\" />",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<img src=\"assets\\ot4_0094_c32fdc35b333.png\" style=\"width: 139px; height: 66px;\" />",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Reaction of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HgSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>dil</mi><mo>.</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> with alkyne gives addition of water as per markonikoff&#39;s rule.</p><p><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CH</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi>CH</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><munderover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>HgSO</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></munderover><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>CHO</mi></math></p><p>Hence, by this process preparation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>CHO</mi></math><br />Cann&#39;t possible.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0094_8f6a929cc885.png\" style=\"width: 429px; height: 348px;\" /></p><p>Hence <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>CHO</mi></math> cannot be formed.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0094_99e2254d5640.png\" style=\"width: 351px; height: 159px;\" /></p>"
  }
}